  "intro": "Design patterns are the vocabulary senior engineers use to describe solutions, and freshers who know them stand out immediately. This module covers the SOLID principles that every professional Java developer follows, plus the most commonly asked GoF patterns: Singleton, Factory, Builder, Strategy, Observer, and Decorator. Each is explained in the context of Spring Boot — so you can answer not just 'what is it' but 'where have you seen it'."
